  "Number": 32,
  "Question": "\\(K\\) takes \\(30\\) minutes less time than \\(M\\) to travel a distance of \\(30\\) miles. \\(K\\) travels \\(\\dfrac13\\) mile per hour faster than \\(M.\\) If \\(x\\) is \\(K\\)’s rate of speed in miles per hour, then \\(K\\)’s time for the distance is:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(\\dfrac{x+\\frac{1}{3}}{30}\\)",
    "B": "\\(\\dfrac{x-\\frac{1}{3}}{30}\\)",
    "C": "\\(\\dfrac{30}{x+\\frac{1}{3}}\\)",
    "D": "\\(\\dfrac{30}{x}\\)",
    "E": "\\(\\dfrac{x}{30}\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "Let \\(t\\) be K's travel time in hours. K travels \\(30\\) miles at \\(x\\) miles per hour, so the relationship distance equals speed times time gives\n\\[\nxt=30.\n\\]\nHere \\(x>0\\), so dividing by \\(x\\) gives\n\\[\nt=\\boxed{\\frac{30}{x}\\text{ hours}}.\n\\]\nThe answer is choice D.",
